A||||6||GWMORGAN||SHUDDERING!!!||||13||
Z||000000||GWMORGAN||04-11-2000||05:49 PM||||Hi All,<BR>Recently,my 86GT with Isuzu 5spd. tranny shudders (engine shakes badly) when I'm at a stop, in 1st gear and the clutch all the way to the floor. Sometimes she refuses to go in 1st gear with the motor running. I have to cut the motor, then put her in gear. All gears are selected freely with the motor off, but have problems going to 1st, from 2nd to 3rd and reverse.<BR>since installing a polyurethane dog-bone, I'm getting a "clunking" sound when moving from a dead stop in 1st gear and shifting to 2nd, which makes me suspect bad lower tranny/engine mount(s). Could that be the reason for the shaking? I suspect two causes for the problem with gear selection (1) Hydraulics or clutch.<BR>Any info before I go spending $$$$$.<BR>Thanks.||||reg||13
Z||000001||Patrick||04-11-2000||06:02 PM||||<BR>I'm not sure about the <I>clunking</I>, but the <I>shuddering</I> certainly sounds familiar. It sounds like clutch hydraulic problems to me. There has been a ton of stuff posted here on this subject, and as you can imagine, various opinions expressed on the matter. I suggest you do a <I>Search</I> and decide for yourself what your next course of action will be.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||04-11-2000||07:21 PM||||yeah, definatly a clutch problem. Likely the front side mounts as well.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Carrolles||04-11-2000||10:56 PM||||Does the clutch disengage real close to the floor?  If so take a lookat the clutch pedal first.  The aluminum ones tend to bend over time and cause the problem you are having.  I believe the replacement steel one is still available from the dealer.<P><BR>If your trans is original to the 86GT then it a Muncie Getrag.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||GWMORGAN||04-12-2000||08:10 AM||||Carrolles...My clutch disengages so close to the floor it's unbelievable. If I just think about it, it will happen (LOL). Sometimes I'm in 1st gear at a dead stop with the clutch all the way to the floor and she "creeps" along with my foot off the brakes, meaning the clutch is still engaged. I have a steel pedal with a '87 Isuzu 5spd tranny.||||reg||13
Z||000005||fieroshop||04-12-2000||11:50 AM||||You might have a bad slave cylinder or a bad master cylinder. Check and see if you have hydraulic oil in the rubber boot. If you do then you need to replace it or them. I had to replace both of my cylinders because they were bad but that did not cure mt problem. Before I opened up shop I was on a trip and my clutch gad gone out. It was replaced by an cheap after market clutch and I just took it out and found that the throwout bearing had eaten itself into the fingers of the pressure plate and that caused it to not release properly. It was releasing just of the floor just like yours. Hope you do not have to replace clutch but be ready. Well this time I am installing one of my clutches that are made for my shop.||||reg||1
Z||000006||GWMORGAN||04-20-2000||02:25 PM||||Problems solved. I replaced the master and slave cylinders and now everything's perfect.<BR>Thanks for all the input guys.<BR>Peace and Love <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||14
